+### PR: Periodic whole-PR architecture and spec review after failed QA rounds
+`pr-b491378` (#288; no registry dependencies; required by [[plan-delivery]] D3 acceptance/handoff and D9 qualification)
+
+After a configurable number of completed aggregate QA runs ending NEEDS_WORK (default two) since the last completed checkpoint, or on a grounded early request, the next review cycle starts with a whole-PR architecture and specification checkpoint. It reviews the original goal, complete diff, spec, accumulated review/QA findings, affected interfaces, user decisions and the owning plan, questions the spec as evidence of intent rather than proof, and records a short evidence-linked assessment (keep, current-PR corrections, spec clarification or proposed change for human approval, scoped follow-up, or a referral to #165). Individual scenario failures, infrastructure retries, incomplete runs and INPUT_REQUIRED waits do not count; a useful fix still counts. Run identity, counts and completion persist across restart and duplicate handoffs; interrupted checkpoints resume with their evidence. NEEDS_WORK semantics, review/QA/sign-off, human gates and the conservative breakup default are unchanged, and `pr-5f4f595`'s final sign-off review of accumulated proposals stays separate. Implementation spec and full-prompt review are required; lifecycle integration follows #241/`pr-1139060`, #247/`pr-1ab9075` and #274/`pr-f0f4129`.
+
